    "name": "M-Walk",
    "description": "M-Walk is a graph-walking agent developed to solve knowledge base completion (KBC), formulated as an RL problem with a known state transition model. It consists of a deep recurrent neural network (RNN) and Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS). The RNN encodes the state (the history of the walked path) and outputs both a policy and Q-values separately. To overcome sparse rewards, M-Walk combines MCTS with the neural policy to generate trajectories that yield more positive rewards. The network is then improved in an off-policy manner using Q-learning on these trajectories, modifying the RNN policy via parameter sharing. The proposed RL algorithm learns by repeatedly applying this policy-improvement step. At test time, MCTS is combined with the neural policy to predict the target node. Experimental results show that M-Walk outperforms other RL-based methods (especially those based on policy gradients) and also surpasses traditional KBC baselines.",
    "keywords": [
        "graph-walking agent",
        "knowledge base completion (KBC)",
        "reinforcement learning (RL)",
        "M-Walk",
        "deep recurrent neural network (RNN)",
        "Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS)",
        "Q-learning"
    ],
